    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on a favorable schedule today, headlined by a high-upside matchup against Merrill Kelly. **Kyle Tucker** (79.51) and **Andy Pages** (74.83) are our strongest plays, as both benefit significantly from the +19% boost provided by Kelly\u2019s lackluster 5.13 xERA. While **Kyle Tucker** remains the focal point for power and speed potential, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.10) also emerges as a high-efficiency start; he holds a distinct platoon advantage against Tyler Mahle, bolstered by a +14% dynamic platoon edge that pushes him comfortably into the Strong category. We are aggressively targeting these matchups to maintain our edge in the scarcity-driven SB category, where players like **Gunnar Henderson** and **Nasim Nunez** remain essential despite varying levels of difficulty against their respective opponents.\n\nThe most difficult benching decision involved **Luis Lara** (47.02), who showed promise but ultimately fell just short of the efficiency threshold required to displace our core starters. While **Luis Lara** remains a solid depth piece, the superior matchup quality for **Wade Meckler** (59.78) and **Jacob Wilson** (59.71)\u2014who are both hitting in the top two spots of their lineups\u2014won out in our optimization. We are monitoring **Gunnar Henderson** closely; his score of 64.29 remains strong, but we have adjusted downward for his matchup against Nathan Eovaldi, who profiles as an elite hold for opposing stolen base attempts. Caution is advised for **Liam Hicks** (41.16), whose score sits dangerously close to the floor due to a tough draw against Logan Gilbert, though he remains in the lineup to ensure we are not burning unnecessary game caps while searching for an optimal C1 configuration.",
